 "notes": "Names not legible on the plate are '?'. (1) The 50 ft north-south street from Otte Street through Philomena to Frederick Avenue (x about 3521-3526) is printed '... ST.' with the name overprinted by pipe labels; it is the same line as Innes (label INNES near y 3100, suffix not read; written Innes Avenue) which continues by a jog to Schneider, Glen Parker and the east-west street at y 3424. (2) The east-west street at y about 3424 from Kirby Avenue east past Innes (addresses 1640-1713; 21 in. sewer) has no name printed inside the strip. (3) The north-south avenue from that street south past Westmoreland, Howland Place, Pullan, Ella to Chase (x 3700-3824) is printed 'AVE.' with an illegible name. (4) The street entering Kirby Avenue from the west at y 1324 is printed only 'ST.' in the strip. (5) The avenue running south-west from the Kirby / Schneider junction (only 'AVE.' printed here) is taken as Virginia Avenue from the VIRGINIA label south of Chase; the avenue from Bruce south to Chase (only 'AVE.' legible) is taken as Florida Avenue, which it joins in line across Chase. Kirby / Schneider / Virginia is one five-armed junction (two entries a few px apart); Kirby / Bruce and Kirby / the y-3424 street are opposite arms 27 px apart; Chase / Pitts and Chase / the unnamed avenue are opposite arms about 30 px apart. Glen Parker Avenue meets Hamilton twice: the west part at (4065,1877) and the part continuing north-east at (4170,1946). Pell / Gordon and Gordon / Howland are L corners. Suffixes of Pitts, Ella, Florida, Innes not read (assumed). JESTER is as printed. Hanfield Street's south side is the plate edge; its centre is taken midway between the north building line and the plate edge. Henry Sr. & Aug. Freudenberg near (2250,2700) is an owner name, not a street. Otte / Hamilton (about 4366,290) and Haight / Hamilton lie east of x 4300 and are not picked."
